<https://fhir-ig.digitalhealth.gov.ng/Basic/NgCoreRegistryService> a fhir:Basic ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "NgCoreRegistryService"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ActorDefinition NgCoreRegistryService</b></p><a name=\"NgCoreRegistryService\"> </a><a name=\"hcNgCoreRegistryService\"> </a><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Actor: NgCoreRegistryService </b></td><td>Nigeria Core Registry Service</td><td>Type: system </td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\"><div><h3>Role</h3>\n<p>The <strong>Nigeria Core Registry Service</strong> provides authoritative or governed\ninformation about entities such as:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>patients or clients;</li>\n<li>practitioners and health workers;</li>\n<li>organisations and health facilities;</li>\n<li>locations and healthcare services;</li>\n<li>pharmacies and laboratories;</li>\n<li>payers, products, devices, or other governed entities.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A Registry Service may operate nationally, subnationally, institutionally, or\nwithin a federated registry architecture.</p>\n<h3>Responsibilities</h3>\n<p>A Registry Service may:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>register entities using applicable Nigeria Core profiles;</li>\n<li>maintain and verify governed identifiers;</li>\n<li>provide authorised lookup and search;</li>\n<li>support matching, duplicate detection, linking, and reconciliation;</li>\n<li>manage updates and status changes;</li>\n<li>preserve appropriate provenance and history; and</li>\n<li>publish supported capabilities.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Typical resource mappings include:</p>\n<table class=\"grid\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Registry domain</th>\n<th>FHIR resource</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Patient/client</td>\n<td><code>Patient</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Health worker</td>\n<td><code>Practitioner</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Practitioner role</td>\n<td><code>PractitionerRole</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Facility/organisation</td>\n<td><code>Organization</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Location</td>\n<td><code>Location</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Caregiver/related person</td>\n<td><code>RelatedPerson</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Service directory</td>\n<td><code>HealthcareService</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3>Conformance expectations</h3>\n<p>A Registry Service <strong>SHALL</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>use applicable Nigeria Core profiles;</li>\n<li>use nationally governed identifiers where defined;</li>\n<li>preserve identifier systems, namespaces, and issuing authorities;</li>\n<li>comply with applicable profile and terminology constraints;</li>\n<li>return FHIR-conformant responses; and</li>\n<li>provide an accurate <code>CapabilityStatement</code> when exposing a FHIR endpoint.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It <strong>SHALL NOT</strong> issue or redefine a nationally governed identifier without the\nauthority to do so.</p>\n<h3>Identity and stewardship</h3>\n<p>Where matching is supported, sufficient identifiers and demographic or other\ngoverned attributes <strong>SHOULD</strong> be used to minimise false matches and duplicate\nregistrations. Algorithmic matching <strong>SHOULD</strong> be governed, tested, and\nauditable.</p>\n<p>Registry governance <strong>SHOULD</strong> define the authoritative source, identifier\nlifecycle, update rules, data-quality controls, access policies, stewardship,\nand duplicate/conflict resolution.</p>\n<p>Access to registry information <strong>SHALL</strong> follow applicable security and privacy\nrequirements according to the sensitivity of the registry domain.</p>\n<h3>Relationships</h3>\n<p>The Registry Service commonly interacts with the <strong>Nigeria Core Requestor,\nResponder, Terminology Service,</strong> and <strong>Conformance and Sandbox Service</strong>.</p>\n<p>A Registry Service may itself act as a Requestor when consulting another\nauthoritative service.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></div>"
  ] ;
